{title: Just Be Held}
{artist: Casting Crowns}
{key: Am}

{comment: Intro}
[Am] [F] [C] [G/D]

{comment: Verse}
[Am]Hold it all together, [F]everybody needs you [C]strong, [G/D]
But life [Am]hits you out of nowhere and [F]barely leaves you holding [C]on  [G/D]
And when you're [Am]tired of [F]fighting, [C]chained by your control [G/D]
There's [Am]freedom in [F]surrender, lay it [C]down and let it [G]go.

{comment: Chorus}

So when you're [C]on your knees and answers seem so [G]far away,
You're not [Am]alone, stop holding on, and just be [F]held,
Your [C]world's not falling apart, it's falling [G]into place
I'm on the [Am]throne, stop holding on, and just be [F]held
Just be [Am]held [F] [C] [G/D]
Just be [Am]held [F] [C] [G/D]

{comment: Verse}

If your [Am]eyes are on the storm, you'll [F]wonder if I love you [C]still  [G/D]
But if your [Am]eyes are on the cross, you [F]know I always have and I [C]always will  [G/D]
And not a [Am]tear is [F]wasted, in [C]time you'll [G/D]understand
I'm painting [Am]beauty with the [F]ashes, your [C]life is in My [G]hands

{comment: Bridge}

Lift your [G/D]hands, lift your [Am]eyes, in the [C]storm is where you'll [F]find Me
And where you [G/D]are, I'll hold your [Am]heart, I'll [C]hold your [G]heart
Come to [G/D]Me, find your [Am]rest,
In the [C]arms of the God who won't let [G]go
